{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Wolf, etc.</b> The meaning is peace. According to the view of many, HaShem will remove the nature of the wolf, and the proof is 'like the ox it shall eat straw.'" "And the meaning of <b>dust shall be the serpent's food</b> — like its nature, and not something else; the meaning is that it shall not harm." "All these prophecies are destined for the land of Israel alone, for thus it is written: 'upon all My holy mountain.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:08.753685133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}